WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.170
Killua

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:11.450
How does a character go from here - to here?
- But maybe, this isn’t even the correct

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:17.250
question to ask here. Because bad guy going
good is not exactly a revolutionary trope

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:23.350
in storytelling. So, maybe the better question
to ask here, is why Killua’s complete change

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:29.539
of character feels so incredibly authentic
and natural and why his story is so strongly

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:33.909
relatable.
There is a reason why Killua Zoldyck is by

00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:40.649
far the most beloved character in a story,
that Yoshihiro Togashi has filled to the brim

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:47.989
with fascinatingly complex &amp; intriguing characters.
Being cool, charismatic and at times a bit

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:53.699
creepy, Killua is already a through and through
enjoyable character, even just at a superficial

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:58.839
level. Being the second protagonist of the
story, we accompany him on his journey with

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:03.140
Gon through the dangerous world of Hunter
x Hunter and enjoy watching him grow stronger

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:11.360
and more mature - a typical shounen adventure.
But, as is the case with almost all characters

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.799
in this beautifully crafted series, you have
to dig just a tiny bit deeper into the structure

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:22.649
of the plot to discover that Killua’s character
is pretty much as complex and multi-layered

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:28.100
as it gets. Killua’s arc contains a number
of underlying themes, that I think are all

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:34.030
worth looking at in detail to truly understand
his character. This includes his quest to

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:38.890
break free from the chains of his family,
developing self-worth, seeking freedom of

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:45.000
will and ultimately finding his purpose in
life - all elements, that Togashi has not

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.990
only connected to the plot at hand and Killua’s
journey through the world, but that he also

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:55.539
has interconnected and woven into each other
to form a complete and organic feeling character

00:01:55.539 --> 00:02:01.039
that is shaped by his upbringing, but also
his environment. As we have discussed in the

00:02:01.039 --> 00:02:06.969
last video, the overall theme of Hunter Hunter
is humanity and what it means to be human

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:12.840
in a superhuman world, and Togashi uses the
classic trope of the buddy story to contrast

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:21.870
both Killua and Gon and their growth and coming-of-age
from a realistic and credible perspective.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:29.659
Thus, instead of going chronologically, which
might feel a bit too much like a recap of

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:34.470
the story, I think it is best to look at the
relationship between Killua and Gon first,

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.799
to give you a better idea of the overall character
and then delve deeper into the details of

00:02:39.799 --> 00:02:45.430
his character arc. Before we can discuss the
dreadfully dramatic dream Team that is Killua

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:50.700
and Gon however, I believe that we have to
first take a closer look at Killua’s upbringing

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:58.890
to really understand how he became the unsettlingly
dark boy we first meet during the hunter exam.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:05.459
Killua’s tragic childhood and the complex
relations within his family are something

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:11.269
that is revealed only in increments by Togashi,
while we travel from arc to arc. While we

00:03:11.269 --> 00:03:15.860
personally get to see his family home and
parts of his relatives in the Zoldyck family

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.629
arc after the hunter exam takes place, many
crucial details surrounding the family are

00:03:20.629 --> 00:03:26.470
revealed in other arcs. Killua’s relationship
with Illumi for instance is introduced during

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:32.090
the hunter exam arc, his grandfather appears
for the first in the Yorknew arc to take out

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:39.409
Chrollo and Alluka is only introduced after
the Chimera Ant arc. If you sometimes feel

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:46.790
a bit confused by all the different relationships
and connections within the Zoldyck family,

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:51.099
this seems to have been done on purpose, as
this panel here illustrates pretty well I

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:57.250
think. Now this incremental introduction of
Killua’s family and all its members serves

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:03.720
two larger purposes I believe, firstly, next
to Killua, several of the Zoldycks generally

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:09.109
play a relevant role in several story arcs
and seem to be a major force in the world,

00:04:09.109 --> 00:04:16.700
politically and militarily. Secondly and more
importantly I think, Togashi slowly shares

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:21.530
more and more information about Killua’s
past and true personality as an essential

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.550
part of his character arc and development,
which we will be discussing in a second. Overall

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:31.970
there are four major themes in Killua’s
past that make him the inhuman person that

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:36.140
we meet at the beginning of the story and
that he needs to overcome throughout his journey

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:45.200
with Gon: Assassination, torture, expectations
&amp; love. So, let’s look at these elements

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:53.920
in a bit more detail.
As the Zoldycks are a family of assassins,

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:59.720
violence and murder are not only part of their
daily business, but of their family identity.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:05.040
Killua was trained and shaped to become a
top tier assassin basically from the moment

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:10.690
that he was born. Growing up in this kind
of environment, Killua has grown numb to the

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:15.200
act of killing, to the point where he even
seems to be getting a bit of enjoyment out

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.710
of it. We can see this for instance in chapter
14 during the Hunter Exam arc, where he grows

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:27.460
frustrated playing ball with Netero and Gon.
At some point he relies more on more on excessive

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:32.930
force, resulting in a kick, that in Netero's
words would be capable of shattering a normal

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:38.460
person's leg. After leaving the game, in his
bloodlust, that had started to overtake him

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:43.410
throughout the match, he releases his frustration
on some unfortunate Hunter examinees that

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:48.621
crossehis path, leaving them dead on the ground
as Killua walks away without so much as a

00:05:48.621 --> 00:05:54.520
second glance at them. Thus, his upbringing
has left him with little regard for the value

00:05:54.520 --> 00:06:07.030
of life and the use of violence against others.As
part of his training and due to the high expectations

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:12.840
in him, Killua was subjected to countless
tortures by the hands of his family when he

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:19.150
was young. As a result, he became immune to
poison, developed a high tolerance to electricity,

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.440
and grew in agility and strength with his
fingernails being able to turn into sharp

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:30.320
claws. But the cruel physical abuse clearly
has left strong marks on him, physically and

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:36.000
mentally. While Killua does in fact try his
best to conceal any signs of the torture and

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.750
cruelty he had to endure all his life, slowly
but steadily we learn more and more about

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:48.140
the horrors he had to endure. From Illumi’s
manipulation, to the scars he carries on his

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:53.670
body that we can see during his training with
Biscuit, we finally understand that the horrible

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:59.040
insight we got into Killua’s childhood in
the family house was apparently only the tip

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:05.080
of the iceberg. Here, we actually get a first
glimpse into this, when Milluki is attempting

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:10.220
to torture Killua after running off to take
the Hunter Exam. The fact that he was brutally

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:15.830
tortured at the hand of his own brother didn’t
seem to bother him at all, neither physically

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:21.290
nor mentally. However, while Killua might
have grown numb to his own abuse, he seems

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:28.080
to understand quite clearly that what has
happened to him was terrible. Once he learned

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:33.030
that Gon, Leorio and Kurapika had come for
him, the very notion that his friends could

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:38.190
be threatened placed Killua in an immediately
aggressive disposition where he appeared more

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:43.240
than willing to attack his own brother - something
that Milluki seemed to immediately pick up

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:50.290
on himself - given his troubled expression.
And while this is only one example out of

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:56.620
many, it already does offer us our first implication
of Killua's cripplingly perverted sense of

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:03.140
self-worth. Having known nothing else his
entire life, Killua didn't mind being tortured,

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:09.730
almost as if he felt that for him to experience
this was only natural and entirely acceptable.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:15.040
And yet he was completely enraged at the thought
that someone else he cared about might have

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:20.820
to endure this very same treatment. So, his
relationship to torture is not only a strong

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:26.390
indicator of Killua’ lack of self-worth,
but also gives a first insight that despite

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:31.960
his cruel past, he still has a natural sense
of morality that lies suppressed under his

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:43.159
numbness - something that his family without
any doubt wished to get rid of. On top of

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:48.959
everything his family did to him or maybe
exactly because of it, Killua also suffers

00:08:48.959 --> 00:08:53.610
under the heavy expectations his parents have
in him for becoming the heir to the family

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:59.880
legacy. The Zoldycks are infamous in the Hunter
world for being top-tier assassins, with some

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:05.620
of the most capable fighters in the story,
and yet within this group of monsters it was

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:11.010
Killua that was chosen to one day take over
the family, because he showed the most potential

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:17.279
out of his siblings, including his brother
Illumi. Despite being a true prodigy in terms

00:09:17.279 --> 00:09:22.339
of fighting and mastering new skills, something
he demonstrates over and over again side by

00:09:22.339 --> 00:09:29.829
side with Gon, Killua has no interest whatsoever
in continuing the family business, which is

00:09:29.829 --> 00:09:35.170
quite understandable given how his family
treated him. And it is one of the reasons

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:40.339
that Killua is looking for his own purpose
in life and makes us readers wonder whether

00:09:40.339 --> 00:09:45.860
or not he actually has a free will of his
own. And this already brings me to the last

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:56.860
theme of Killua’s childhood: Love. As we
will see again later on in this video, expressing

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:02.339
affection and love is something that Killua
is struggling with throughout the story and

00:10:02.339 --> 00:10:07.839
is something he has to learn more about first.
Throughout large parts of the story, Killua

00:10:07.839 --> 00:10:13.470
only knows how to show his love for others
by protecting them: Killua tried to protect

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:19.430
Gon countless times during their journey and
was reduced to tears at the thought of failing,

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:25.790
he stood up for Zushi and he even initiated
his friendship with Ikalgo by saving his life,

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:31.980
only to name a few examples. His inexperience
with expressing such emotions comes from the

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:37.470
twisted sense of love that he has experienced
from mostly his mother Kikyo and his brother

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:43.529
Illumi. Kikyo was willing to literally chain
Killua down and beat him if it meant keeping

00:10:43.529 --> 00:10:51.600
him "safe”, at least in her eyes. Illumi
meanwhile, in his over-protective and psychopathic

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:57.100
way, went so far as to implant one of his
manipulative Nen needles into Killua without

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:02.520
his knowledge or consent giving him subconscious
orders that dictated his actions throughout

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:10.670
most off the series. Both of their abusive
shows of affection for Killua have most likely

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:17.120
accompanied him all his life and based on
nothing but his own innate sense of morality,

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:24.189
protecting was the only thing he knew to do.
And so, these four elements, assassination,

00:11:24.189 --> 00:11:30.589
torture, expectations and love are what I
believe have made Killua the physically strong

00:11:30.589 --> 00:11:36.509
and emotionally broken kid that Gon meets
at the hunter entrance exam, and I think that

00:11:36.509 --> 00:11:44.130
the Zoldyck family home does a wonderful job
of symbolising all this. The inside of the

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:50.150
house is more akin to a medieval castle decked
out with a modern security system, a torture

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:56.529
room and even a secret room to hide his sister.
Being atop a mountain, it’s quite isolated

00:11:56.529 --> 00:12:00.439
and because of the numerous safeguards and
obstacles that separate outsiders from the

00:12:00.439 --> 00:12:06.019
family, starting with the Testing Gate, it’s
also easy to see why Killua never had any

00:12:06.019 --> 00:12:12.160
friends until he met Gon, assassins’ training
and duties aside, making it painfully clear

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:17.899
why Killua wanted to break free from his family
so badly.&nbsp;Based on the theme of humanity

00:12:17.899 --> 00:12:23.209
and the realistic approach Hunter x Hunter
takes on people, it is only understandable

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:29.689
then, that Killua ended up with such a dark,
twisted and insecure perspective after experiencing

00:12:29.689 --> 00:12:35.620
so much physical and emotional abuse. And
so I think it is more than fair to say that

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:41.800
the Zoldyck family is the main source of Killua's
need for finding free will, self-worth and

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:47.559
a purpose in life. And so, now that we know
this underlying psychological background,

00:12:47.559 --> 00:12:53.740
let’s now look at what happened when Togashi
threw this character into the hunter world.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:58.930
And what better place to start than the most
important relationship in the story, his friendship

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:05.100
with Gon.
We already talked a little bit about the relationship

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:10.430
between Gon and Killua in the last video.
However, I purposefully decided to save the

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:16.060
majority of it for today, since I think we
need some understanding of both Gon AND Killua

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:20.889
so wen can truly understand and appreciate
their connection in full. The main thing I

00:13:20.889 --> 00:13:25.970
think, that makes the friendship between Gon
and Killua so special, is that they have completely

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:33.300
mirrored character arcs - one negative and
the other positive. Gon goes from joyful and

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:39.439
caring at the beginning of the story to numb,
cruel and inhuman towards the end. Killua

00:13:39.439 --> 00:13:45.649
meanwhile goes from numb, cruel and inhuman
to joyful and caring. And so, while Gon’s

00:13:45.649 --> 00:13:51.149
lowest point is close towards the end of the
story in his brutal murder of Pitou, Killua’s

00:13:51.149 --> 00:13:55.759
lowest point in the story is pretty close
towards the beginning, at the end of the hunter

00:13:55.759 --> 00:14:01.740
exam. First, as we already mentioned he kills
some of the other hunter examines simply out

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:07.939
of annoyance and bloodlust. And later, during
the final stage, he ends up failing the hunter

00:14:07.939 --> 00:14:13.160
exam overall for killing another contender,
manipulated by Illumi and being recaptured

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:19.350
by the claws of his family. He leaves behind
Gon and goes back home with his will and dreams

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:25.879
once again broken. This state of complete
surrender to his family and the cruel act

00:14:25.879 --> 00:14:31.949
of murder he commits are the absolute bottom
point for Killua in the entire series, and

00:14:31.949 --> 00:14:39.019
from this point onward his arc is on a constant
incline. Ironically enough, it was Gon’s

00:14:39.019 --> 00:14:45.180
friendship and original morality that saved
Killua, and Gon’s later moral decline encourages

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:51.339
Killua to question his own morality and views.
Both Gon and Killua had to grow up with no

00:14:51.339 --> 00:14:56.620
friends around them and both of them want
to travel the world and become stronger. Thus

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:01.770
the hunter exam was the perfect arc format
to quickly establish a friendship between

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:07.439
these two characters right at the start of
the story in a believable way. Since both

00:15:07.439 --> 00:15:12.390
of them were the youngest contenders in a
contest meant for adults, they naturally found

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:18.740
each other, while at the same time highlighting
their uniqueness. While Gon immediately sees

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:24.360
Killua as his friend, given his past and low
sense of self-worth Killua seems to feel like

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:30.179
he has to earn Gon’s friendship first. Thus,
during the final examination he reveals that

00:15:30.179 --> 00:15:36.089
all he wants is “for Gon to be his friend!”
without realising that it’s a) not something

00:15:36.089 --> 00:15:42.350
he needs to ask for and b) that Gon already
considered him his best friend at that point.

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:46.990
And even though Leorio tells him that he already
is Gon’s friend, under the influence of

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:52.819
his brother, Killua’s spirit breaks and
he sees his dream crushed. In the despair

00:15:52.819 --> 00:15:57.490
that overtook him in his brother’s presence,
he apparently defaults to the only thing he’d

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:03.869
ever known in his life, and he kills Botero
in cold blood - without Gon there to stop

00:16:03.869 --> 00:16:11.170
him, ultimately returning home, certain that
he after all has no will of his own. And when

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:17.160
Killua is literally chained up again inside
his family home, it once again is Gon who

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:22.740
comes to save him and take him out into the
world - showing Killua that he now truly has

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:29.589
made a real friend. Gon is Killua’s light
in the dark, something that he makes very

00:16:29.589 --> 00:16:42.939
clear in this moment here. This - is probably
one of my favourite scenes in the story. It

00:16:42.939 --> 00:16:47.801
brings us back to the start of the adventure
before going into the dark part of the chimera

00:16:47.801 --> 00:16:54.389
ant arc. It’s just one of many moments where
Killua finds himself the most worthless person

00:16:54.389 --> 00:17:00.300
in the world, all while believing that Gon
would be able to lead him to a better life.

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:05.900
And throughout the story, Gon does exactly
that. Gon teaches Killua how to engage in

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:10.790
healthy interactions with other people, how
to express love in different ways, and offers

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:16.550
him a motivation for self-improvement. It
was this motivation that lead Killua to master

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:22.080
Nen and Hatsu to the incredible degree he
does, and ultimately to remove the needle

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:28.991
planted in him by Illumi - finally allowing
his true personality to shine through. Despite

00:17:28.991 --> 00:17:34.550
his creeping decline into darkness, for the
kid who came from darkness in the first place,

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:39.760
Gon indeed served as a light to help Killua
navigate it and turn on his own inner light

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:46.000
switch. And ultimately, I think that Killua
seems to have learned from Gon's influence

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:52.610
on himself of being a light to his darkness.
Because, towards the end, we find that Killua

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:58.680
has now taken on the role of being a light
for Alluka. And so, while Gon’s character

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:04.910
arc followed the path of a tragedy, Killua’s
much rather was a journey of redemption. Thus,

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:10.720
Gon’s falling character arc and Killua’s
rising one slowly approach each other until

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:16.570
they finally cross paths during the Greed
island arc, where I would argue both are roughly

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:22.520
on the same moral level and the two boys are
the closest and most similar to each other.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:27.160
With the beginning of the Chimera Ant arc
however, we see a rapid alienation between

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:33.560
the two. Gon’s arc starts spiralling into
darkness, while Killua’s has a sudden uptake

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:39.410
after removing Illumi’s needle. During the
arc, Gon and Killua’s relationship reaches

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:44.400
its climax and so, despite Killua’s alien
position to the audience at the start of the

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:49.070
series as a young assassin from the notorious
Zoldyck family, he quickly becomes a far easier

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:55.490
reference point than Gon. He starts to see
nuance in situations where Gon only sees his

00:18:55.490 --> 00:19:01.930
own twisted sense of black and white. Killua
is the one to save Gon from being killed by

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:07.420
the Chimera Ant early in the arc while Gon
fully unprepared throws himself into combat

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:12.830
in order to get revenge for the death of his
friend. Liberated from Illumi’s influence

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:17.870
and with his new-found sense of free will
and independence, Killua begins to understand

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:22.510
the complex sense of justice and morality
that the world of&nbsp;Hunter x Hunter&nbsp;operates

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:29.700
on, and increasingly grows worried about Gon’s
single-minded, inflexible approach. When Gon

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:34.760
is supposed to show his resolve to Morel,
he visualizes all the hate and negative emotions

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:41.820
inside him to fuel a frightening attack. In
the last moment, Killua steps in and manages

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:51.531
to pull Gon back from the brink, looking seriously
worried for his friend. Later however, as

00:19:51.531 --> 00:19:57.450
Gon vows to kill the innocent bystander Komugi
to get a shot at Pitou for killing Kite, Killua

00:19:57.450 --> 00:20:03.370
isn’t able to reach his friend anymore.
Because at this point, Gon doesn’t understand

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:09.310
Killuass true feelings anymore, as he demonstrated
so touchingly after the hunter exam. And so,

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:20.060
when Killua finally reaches him and Pitou,
Gon says this. We can see Killua visibly tensing

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:26.750
up here and being deeply hurt by Gon’s words.
And so, once Gon snaps and trades in his remaining

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:34.300
humanity for violence, Killua fully abandons
his cruel past but still is unable to do anything

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:41.770
but watch in horror. After saving Gon’s
life, both boys decide to go their own ways

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:47.700
and it truly feels like something significant
has changed. It’s a departure in every sense

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:53.330
of the word, and the lingering final shot
of two opposing Gungi pieces overlapping each

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:59.990
other fades away it feels almost impossible
to reconcile the beginning of the show with

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:05.410
the end, with both of them having switched
places.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:12.740
I think by now we are starting to get a pretty
good idea of Killua and what It is that drives

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:18.050
his character. Killua’s behaviour and actions
over the course of their journey are quite

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:22.870
different from Gon’s, something I think
Togashi wonderfully explains through their

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:32.950
Nen types. Gon is an enhancer, who are simple
and determined. Most of them never lie, hide

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:37.450
nothing, and are very straightforward in their
actions or in their thinking. Their words

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:42.390
and actions are often dominated by their feelings.
They are generally very selfish and focused

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:49.690
on their goals, something that basically describes
Gon pretty perfectly. The same goes for Killua

00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:55.530
being a transmuter type. They&nbsp;are whimsical,
prone to deceit, and fickle and many tend

00:21:55.530 --> 00:22:01.810
to hide their true intentions.This fits Killua
pretty well. After all, who other than a whimsical

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:10.800
Transmuter could be expected to spend 200
million jenny on snacks? Additionally, Killua

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:16.460
is not opposed to lying. Being the genuinely
well-meaning person that he is, he only lies

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:23.210
when necessary as observed by Bisky, yet he
does lie nonetheless. The most notable trait

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:29.010
here however is his extreme inclination to
conceal information. As expressed near the

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:34.320
end of the Yorknew Arc, Killua will choose
to remain ignorant rather than ask a question

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:39.370
that shows his ignorance to others - being
grateful that Gon asked the questions he was

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:45.760
reluctant to. Additionally, despite admiring
Gon so much, he tends to withhold most of

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:50.850
his feeling on thoughts from him. Thus Killua
is quickly embarrassed when Gon draws attention

00:22:50.850 --> 00:22:56.050
to their friendship, as the true value of
their bond is something Killua prefers to

00:22:56.050 --> 00:23:01.740
keep to himself. The finest example of this
is his heart-wrenching plea to Palm to help

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:06.870
Gon out of his dark mindset. According to
the narrator Killua had intended to lie, here

00:23:06.870 --> 00:23:12.830
as well and conceal his true feelings - yet
in a moment of emotional desperation let it

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:22.650
slip. This short act of opening up was so
powerful for him that he simply couldn't conceal

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:28.640
anything in this moment, breaking down into
tears and begging. Also, since many Transmuters

00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:33.150
rely on techniques that give unique and unpredictable
properties to their Nen that reflect their

00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:37.580
personalities - something we’ll also be
exploring in the next video on Hisoka - I

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:42.850
think Killua’s electricity powers are also
a wonderful representation of his past and

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:48.250
growth at the same time. And so I think it’s
finally time to look at Killua’s character

00:23:48.250 --> 00:23:57.490
arc and how his character has developed over
the course of the story.

00:23:57.490 --> 00:24:03.480
Differently than Gon, Killua starts into the
story without a clear desire or purpose. His

00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:08.830
original desire was to break free from his
family and find his own path, yet since he

00:24:08.830 --> 00:24:14.960
manages to do that relatively early on, he
then lacks any specific goal and thus accompanies

00:24:14.960 --> 00:24:21.220
Gon on his journey to find his father. That
doesn’t mean that he doesn’t have a drive

00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:26.370
though. As we have discussed before, on a
more subconscious level, Killua’s need is

00:24:26.370 --> 00:24:32.000
to break free form his brother’s control
to regain his free will, find self-worth and

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:39.030
ultimately a purpose in life, a philosophy
called Ikigai in Japanese.

00:24:39.030 --> 00:24:43.460
We have already discussed large parts of the
first half of the story, except for the Orkney

00:24:43.460 --> 00:24:48.130
Arc, where Killua is prepared to sacrifice
himself so that Gon can escape the phantom

00:24:48.130 --> 00:24:53.730
troupe. What I really want to focus on however,
is Killua’s moment of revelation and the

00:24:53.730 --> 00:25:02.900
climax of his arc, the emotional battle with
the chimera ant Rammot. Seeing his friend

00:25:02.900 --> 00:25:07.870
be on the verge of death, Killua’s will
to save Gon comes into conflict with his brothers

00:25:07.870 --> 00:25:14.150
orders to run away from any wrong opponent.
After once again apologising to Gon for not

00:25:14.150 --> 00:25:20.250
being of any use, the friendship and love
he has built towards Gon overpower his brother’s

00:25:20.250 --> 00:25:24.340
powers and he is able to remove the needle
that he wasn’t even aware of until that

00:25:24.340 --> 00:25:32.450
point. This scene has some striking implications
for Killua, presents the moment of redemption,

00:25:32.450 --> 00:25:38.510
and it touches upon all of the themes surrounding
his character. Are we slaves to our birth,

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:45.220
to our genetics, the way our families brought
us up, or the lack of a family? Or, by sheer

00:25:45.220 --> 00:25:50.460
force of will and concentrated effort can
we choose to become something different than

00:25:50.460 --> 00:25:56.400
what we were and surpass the limitations set
by our upbringing? It's a very personal issue

00:25:56.400 --> 00:26:02.830
that ultimately culminates into one central
question: how much agency do we actually have

00:26:02.830 --> 00:26:09.440
in our own lives? The needle suddenly gives
us a whole lot of answers about Killua’s

00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:15.350
behaviour that have haunted us the entire
series. Finally realising that Killua was

00:26:15.350 --> 00:26:20.890
being constantly Manipulated by Illumi suddenly
makes his gruesome choice to kill Bodoro a

00:26:20.890 --> 00:26:30.520
bit more understandable. Killua was overwhelmed,
confused, struggling to overcome this subconscious

00:26:30.520 --> 00:26:37.000
urge while remaining faithful to his friends.
Feeling caught by his brother and uncertain

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:43.630
of Leorio's chances, Killua decided to gave
up his chances to become a hunter to help

00:26:43.630 --> 00:26:50.250
Leorio achieve his dream. his lack of self-worth
also played a role in this choice I believe,

00:26:50.250 --> 00:26:55.710
allowing all of his friends but himself to
become a Hunter. And so it is not only a very

00:26:55.710 --> 00:27:01.640
cathartic moment for us readers, but also
for Killua himself to find out that his fear

00:27:01.640 --> 00:27:08.180
&amp; uselessness was actually caused by Illumi's
Hatsu and not due to his cowardice. As it

00:27:08.180 --> 00:27:12.690
turns out, there never was anything wrong
with Killua in the first place - showing us

00:27:12.690 --> 00:27:18.840
that he was actually the best friend anyone
could wish for, being as loyal and dependable

00:27:18.840 --> 00:27:24.570
in spite of the literal mind control trying
to push him away. And I think that this moment

00:27:24.570 --> 00:27:29.950
gives as an even deeper insight into Killua’s
personality. In one regard, it allows us to

00:27:29.950 --> 00:27:35.900
see just how far Killua will go for those
he loves. While captured by the Phantom troupe,

00:27:35.900 --> 00:27:41.440
surrounded on all sides by some of the most
infamous and dangerous Nen users in the world,

00:27:41.440 --> 00:27:46.200
Killua still instinctively began to intervene
in Gon's mistreatment until Hisoka stopped

00:27:46.200 --> 00:27:55.390
him. We can only imagine what pressure Killua
must have felt due to the needle in this situation,

00:27:55.390 --> 00:28:00.050
how many escape plans were running through
his mind, and yet he was ready to stand up

00:28:00.050 --> 00:28:06.700
for his friend in need. For me, this alone
establishes Killua as one of the most protective,

00:28:06.700 --> 00:28:12.990
caring, and self-sacrificing characters in
the all of manga. And what I find important

00:28:12.990 --> 00:28:19.380
to note here, is that this moment is not the
end for his character arc, but rather a knot

00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:25.300
that finally enabled Killua to grow way faster
than before, actually steepening his arc even

00:28:25.300 --> 00:28:30.370
more. In the events that follow this scene,
we see Killua stand up to the Royal Guard,

00:28:30.370 --> 00:28:35.830
chase down Gon-San, challenge his family,
protect Alluka, and see to Gon's healing.

00:28:35.830 --> 00:28:40.490
A true snowball effect of greater and greater
displays of determination, intelligence, and

00:28:40.490 --> 00:28:47.930
loyalty only made possible by allowing Killua
to finally be himself. Killua held back by

00:28:47.930 --> 00:28:53.880
Illumi’s needle was caught in darkness,
outshone by Gon's light. Once it was removed

00:28:53.880 --> 00:28:58.510
however, Killua proved in every way to be
the one shining by far the brightest in their

00:28:58.510 --> 00:29:03.370
friendship from that point onward. While Gon
removes himself from all his friends around

00:29:03.370 --> 00:29:08.520
him more and more after Kite’s death, Killua
forms countless new relationship over the

00:29:08.520 --> 00:29:14.490
course of the chimera ant arc. This goes so
far, that he even befriends one of the ants

00:29:14.490 --> 00:29:19.330
itself. Being part of the enemy group, Ikalgo
would have been straightaway killed if this

00:29:19.330 --> 00:29:24.940
was Hunter Exam Killua, operating under the
standard practices of the family business.

00:29:24.940 --> 00:29:30.860
However at this point, Killua has developed
such a strong sense of morality, compassion

00:29:30.860 --> 00:29:36.060
and nuanced decision making that he understands
the ant’s complex situation and ultimately

00:29:36.060 --> 00:29:42.430
saves him - exactly the development that Gon
failed to make in this arc. As a result Killua

00:29:42.430 --> 00:29:47.750
not only makes a friend, but his kindness
is repaid almost immediately when Ikalgo saves

00:29:47.750 --> 00:29:54.470
him after an unsettlingly dangerous game of
darts. The growth Killua undergoes in this

00:29:54.470 --> 00:29:59.279
arc is even reflected in his fighting. When
Killua unveils his ultimate&nbsp;hatsu&nbsp;technique

00:29:59.279 --> 00:30:06.600
- Godspeed, on Youpi, who previously was way
stronger than him, it is a striking sign of

00:30:06.600 --> 00:30:17.390
how much his character and thus his skills
have grown. While it’s true that Killua

00:30:17.390 --> 00:30:22.410
was always a prodigy - able to learn new skills
way faster than normal, and that his cruel

00:30:22.410 --> 00:30:27.440
childhood gave him a physical advantage in
other ways, it was his journey with Gon and

00:30:27.440 --> 00:30:33.200
ultimately his own innate will and humanity
that enabled one of my favourite character

00:30:33.200 --> 00:30:38.240
arcs in general.
And so with the end of the chimera arc, Killua

00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:43.110
has finally found his sense of self-worth
and his free will. The only things left for

00:30:43.110 --> 00:30:48.630
his arc were breaking fully free from his
family and finding a purpose in life. And

00:30:48.630 --> 00:30:54.150
ironically enough, once again it is Gon who
enables this change. Being on the verge of

00:30:54.150 --> 00:30:59.960
death after his inhuman transformation, Killua
travels home to ask his little sister Alluka

00:30:59.960 --> 00:31:05.630
and the something living inside her to heal
Gon’s wounds. Fittingly to their opposed

00:31:05.630 --> 00:31:11.220
character arcs, Killua is the main protagonist
of this last arc in the story, being a much

00:31:11.220 --> 00:31:16.990
more relatable hero than Gon was towards the
end. Freeing and traveling with his sister,

00:31:16.990 --> 00:31:22.070
Killua finally realises that she is his new
purpose in life and that he can be for Alluka

00:31:22.070 --> 00:31:33.580
and Nanika what Gon was for him: A light in
the darkness. And so at the end of his arc,

00:31:33.580 --> 00:31:38.910
when he parts ways with Gon to travel with
his sister, Killua has found what Gon has

00:31:38.910 --> 00:31:45.490
lost: his humanity and similar to Gon, his
character arc has basically found a complete

00:31:45.490 --> 00:31:51.220
end at this point. So should Killua ever return
in to the story, he will need a new arc as

00:31:51.220 --> 00:31:57.150
well. The powerful message Togashi is sending
with his character is that you are not bound

00:31:57.150 --> 00:32:01.910
by your upbringing but have the freedom to
forge your own path, and that morality and

00:32:01.910 --> 00:32:11.970
humanity is something that can bloom even
under the harshest circumstances.

00:32:11.970 --> 00:32:16.930
So now that we have discussed the mirror of
Gon’s extreme negative and Killua’s extreme

00:32:16.930 --> 00:32:22.310
positive arc, in the next video I want to
discuss a character with a flat character

00:32:22.310 --> 00:32:27.920
arc. It is one of the most iconic figures
in Anime and Manga and for a very good reason

00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:36.680
often used as the face of the series. Im of
course talking about Hisoka and one of the

00:32:36.680 --> 00:32:43.180
most creative antagonists I know. So, stay
tuned for that. Okay, wow I’ve been rambling

00:32:43.180 --> 00:32:46.270
forever now. Thanks guys, peace.

